<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SYNTHETIC CONTOUR MAP — FOR UNIT TESTING ONLY
  ==============================================
  This file does NOT represent any real-world location.
  It was generated programmatically to exercise the contour analysis pipeline.

  Terrain description:
    - A simple bowl/valley shape centred at (0.05, 0.05) degrees.
    - Contours at 100, 105, 110, 115, 120, 125 m elevation.
    - 100 m is the lowest, innermost contour (valley floor).
    - 125 m is the highest, outermost contour (ridge).
    - The terrain naturally drains toward the low-elevation centre.
    - Suitable for testing: interpolation, D8 flow, catchment delineation.

  Spatial extent:  0.00 – 0.10 lon,  0.00 – 0.10 lat  (~11 km x 11 km)
  Contour interval: 5 m
  CRS: WGS84 (EPSG:4326)
-->
